205196075,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":95.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0012273890755639671,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":98.5,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06074438526983761,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":15.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08058776219373387,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":65.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0243072765798291,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":38.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.000963566683280126,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":48.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010954666143131049,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":81.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.03624,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":24.2,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"First Financial Bankshares, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides banking services in the United States. The company offers general commercial banking services, including checking, savings and time deposits, loans, automated teller machines, drive-in and night deposit services, safe deposit facilities, remote deposit capture, internet banking, mobile banking, payroll cards, funds transfer, and other customary commercial banking service, as well as securities brokerage services. It also provides personal trust services, such as wealth management; administration of estates, oil and gas management; farm and ranch; property management; testamentary trusts; revocable and irrevocable trusts; and agency accounts. In addition, the company offers commercial and industrial; municipal; agricultural; construction and development; farm; residential; consumer auto and non-auto; and non-owner occupied and owner occupied commercial real estate loans. Further, it provides advice and specialized services related to lending, investing, purchasing, advertising, public relations, and technology services. First Financial Bankshares, Inc. was founded in 1890 and is headquartered in Abilene, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David W. Bailey | CEO & President | Age 41 | Compensation: $996,970 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $421K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $191K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["First Financial Bankshares, Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.4B market cap on $632M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $286M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 45 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 20% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"First Financial Bankshares (NASDAQ:FFIN) Stock: Insider Murray Hamilton Edwards Acquires 800 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/first-financial-bankshares-nasdaqffin-stock-insider-murray-hamilton-edwards-acquires-800-shares.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793875153.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"First Financial Bankshares (NASDAQ:FFIN) and Hanmi Financial (NASDAQ:HAFC) Critical Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/first-financial-bankshares-nasdaqffin-and-hanmi-financial-nasdaqhafc-critical-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793874584.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Murray Hamilton Edwards Acquires 800 Shares of FFIN Stock via Trust Transactions","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/murray-hamilton-edwards-acquires-800-shares-of-ffin-stock-via-trust-transactions","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793717291.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"How (FFIN) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/How_FFIN_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_110126052602_1793528762.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793528762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"First Financial Bankshares Reports Q3 2026 Net Income of $74.3 Million","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"htt